---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const title = "Trademark Application Process in India: Step-by-Step | BRNDNUR";
const description = "Understand the complete lifecycle of a trademark application in India: Form TM-A drafting, examination, opposition period, and registration certificate issuance.";
const canonical = "https://brndnur.com/resources/trademark-application-process/";
---

<BaseLayout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  canonical={canonical}
  currentPath="/resources/trademark-application-process/"
>
  <main id="main-content">
    <section class="page-hero">
      <div class="container">
        <p class="eyebrow">Procedural Guide</p>
        <h1>The Trademark Application Process in India: Step-by-Step.</h1>
        <p class="lead">A complete walk-through of the statutory application stages from Form TM-A electronic filing to final registration certificate issuance.</p>
        <div class="actions">
          <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/trademark-registration/">Start Registration &rarr;</a>
          <a class="btn btn-outline" href="/resources/">Back to Resources</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <div class="container">
        <article class="legal-prose">
          <div class="legal-box">
            <strong>Timeline Notice:</strong> While e-filing produces an immediate application number and filing receipt, statutory examination, public advertising, and certificate issuance typically require 6 to 12 months, depending on registry workload and whether objections arise.
          </div>

          <h2>Stage 1: Filing Form TM-A (Day 1)</h2>
          <p>The application is submitted electronically through the IP India e-filing portal. Upon successful payment of government fees, an official filing receipt containing your 7-digit Application Number is generated. From this moment, you are legally permitted to affix the &trade; symbol to your mark.</p>

          <h2>Stage 2: Formalities Check Pass & Vienna Codification (1–3 Months)</h2>
          <p>The Trade Marks Registry verifies that all essential documentation (Power of Attorney Form TM-48, user affidavit if claiming prior use, and MSME/incorporation certificates) is attached. If logo artwork is submitted, it is assigned Vienna Classification codes based on international figurative guidelines.</p>

          <h2>Stage 3: Substantive Examination (3–6 Months)</h2>
          <p>A designated Trademark Examiner evaluates the mark against statutory criteria:</p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Section 9 Objections:</strong> Raised if the mark is non-distinctive, descriptive of goods/services, or deceptive.</li>
            <li><strong>Section 11 Objections:</strong> Raised if the mark is identical or confusingly similar to earlier registered or pending marks in the same or related classes.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>If objections are cited, an official Examination Report is issued, and a formal written reply must be filed within 30 days.</p>

          <h2>Stage 4: Show Cause Hearing (If Required)</h2>
          <p>If the Examiner is not fully convinced by the written reply, a Show Cause Hearing is scheduled before an Assistant Registrar. Submissions are made regarding distinctiveness, market goodwill, or differences from cited marks.</p>

          <h2>Stage 5: Journal Publication & 4-Month Opposition Window</h2>
          <p>Once accepted, the mark is advertised in the official Trade Marks Journal (published weekly on the IP India portal). Third parties have exactly 4 months from the publication date to file a notice of opposition (Form TM-O). If no opposition is received within this 4-month window, the mark proceeds to registration.</p>

          <h2>Stage 6: Registration Certificate Issuance</h2>
          <p>The Registry issues the digital Certificate of Registration under the seal of the Trade Marks Registry. The owner may now replace the &trade; symbol with the &reg; registered trademark symbol.</p>

          <h2>Stage 7: 10-Year Renewals and Maintenance</h2>
          <p>Trademark registration remains in effect for 10 years from the original application date. It can be renewed indefinitely every 10 years by filing Form TM-R with the statutory renewal fee.</p>
        </article>

        <div class="cta-panel" style="margin-top: 48px;">
          <p class="eyebrow">Professional Representation</p>
          <h2>Navigate the Registration Journey with Confidence.</h2>
